B{€µÇÈ÷/b…†²ŞßCt¨©ªÅÆêëìÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀INTRODUCTION TO CONFIGURE␀ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀Configuration is the process of describing your computer␀hardware and setting program preferences.  Some of the␀configuration items, such as your types of floppy␀drives, are needed before you can make backups.␀Other configuration items, like program colors, are only␀preferences and do not impact the backup process.␀␀When you install Backup on your computer, you will be␀guided through the configuration steps automatically.␀You can view specific help relating to each step by␀pressing F1.␀␀After you have installed and configured Backup, you can␀change any of the configuration settings at any time by␀choosing the Configure button in the Main Program dialog␀box.␀␀When you are finished with a Configure session, you␀have two choices:␀␀		You can choose OK.  If you exit	from Backup␀        without saving the configuration, the next time␀        you start Backup, it will be configured as␀        it was before the changes.␀␀		This is useful if you want to try out the␀		changes you have made before saving them.␀␀		You can choose Save, and the changes you have␀		made will be saved in the MSBACKUP.INI file. The␀		changes will take effect immediately, and they␀		will remain in effect each time you use␀		Backup.␀␀␀For more information, see:␀␀	|␀Using the Configure Dialog Box|␀␀␀␀;␀x␀±␀Ğ␀	BC[\½òÿ␀L¹ŞßEt¢£¾¿ó$12;<r¨×ãäR‚ƒŠ‹ºî$]’Ÿ «¬áDNOPÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀USING THE CONFIGURE	DIALOG BOX␀ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀The Configure dialog box contains the following buttons:␀␀  ş	|␀Video and Mouse|␀␀	Choose this button to set video options, such as␀	colors and number of display lines, and mouse␀	options, such as cursor movement and right or left-␀	handed use.␀␀  ş	|␀Backup Devices|␀␀	With Backup you can back up to floppy disks or any␀    device or drive that can be accessed as a MS-DOS␀    path. Choose the Backup Devices button to configure␀    Backup to work with your drives.␀␀	If you add or change a backup device, first choose␀	the Backup Devices button and select the device.␀	Then choose the Compatibility Test button and␀	perform a compatibility test for the device.␀␀  ş	|␀Compatibility Test|␀␀	Choose this button to perform a Compatibility Test␀    to ensure your backup devices work with this␀    program.␀␀  ş	Save␀␀	Choose this button to save the configuration on your␀	hard disk.  The changes will take effect immediately␀	and will be in effect the next time you start␀    Backup.␀␀	When you are configuring Backup for the first time,␀    you should choose Save.  Otherwise, you will have to␀    go through the configuration process again.␀␀  ş	OK␀␀	Choose this button if you want to try out any␀	changes you have made to the configuration without␀	saving them.  If you exit from Backup without saving␀    the configuration, the next time you start Backup it␀    will be configured as it was before you made the␀    changes.␀␀  ş	Cancel␀␀	Choose this button if you do not want to change the␀	configuration.  None of the selections you made in␀	any of the Configuration dialog boxes will be␀	applied.␀␀␀␀•␀,e†¿ñFOPˆ´µç,EFw‘ÁçòóCgh¸ÆÇó	
