0]^_—¸¹ëK}½¾í<cdÂìíPz{ªØìíKvw¦ÕBoœÏ ;<bcdÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀USING THE KEYBOARD AND THE MOUSE␀ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀Backup works equally well with your keyboard or a␀Microsoft compatible mouse.␀␀ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀KEYBOARD␀␀  Every function, option and menu can be activated with␀  a hotkey shortcut or by using the cursor.␀␀  In general, the following keys perform standard␀  functions within Backup:␀␀	Tab			Moves the cursor to the next area␀				within a dialog box.␀␀	Shift-Tab	Moves the cursor to the previous area␀				within a dialog box.␀␀	Arrow key	Moves the cursor to the closest item␀				or button in the direction of the␀				arrow.␀␀				When in a text box, use RightArrow and␀				LeftArrow to move the cursor one␀				character to the left or right.␀␀				When in a list box, use UpArrow and␀				DownArrow to move the cursor within␀				the list.␀␀				NOTE:  To move the cursor out of a list␀					   box, use Tab.␀␀				When in a menu, use RightArrow and␀				LeftArrow to open another menu.  Use␀				UpArrow and DownArrow to move the␀				cursor between menu items.␀␀	Enter		Chooses the default button.  The␀				default button has arrows, like␀				this:␀␀					ÚÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ¿␀					³        OK          ³␀					ÀÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÙ␀␀				When you press Enter from any point␀				within a dialog box, the default button␀				is chosen.␀␀	Spacebar	Selects and deselects check boxes,␀				radio buttons and list items, including␀				directories and files.␀␀	Home		Moves the cursor to the beginning of␀				a list or an edit box.␀␀	End			Moves the cursor to the end of a list␀				or an edit box.␀␀	PgUp		Moves the cursor to the top of a list␀				in window-size increments.␀␀	PgDn		Moves the cursor to the bottom of a␀				list in window-size increments.␀␀	F1			Displays context-sensitive help.␀␀	Esc			Cancels the current operation, closes␀				the current dialog box without saving␀				changes, and returns to the previous␀				dialog box.␀␀				Cancels the active menu without making␀				a selection.␀␀	Hotkey		Most commands and options in dialog␀				boxes have a character which appears␀				highlighted or in a contrasting	color.␀				These letters are called hotkeys, and␀				can be used to select the item.␀␀				To quickly select an item on the screen␀				which contains a hotkey, press the␀				hotkey letter.␀␀				In some cases you have to hold down␀				the Alt key to activate a hotkey. This␀                is necessary when the cursor is in␀				a list box, since pressing a key in a␀				list box initiates a search of the list.␀␀␀ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀MOUSE␀␀  With the mouse you can:␀␀		Configure the mouse sensitivity, acceleration,␀		double-click rate, and button usage for left-␀		or right-handed users.  Choose Configure from␀		the Main Program dialog box to change the mouse␀		configuration.␀␀		Select all items by pointing and clicking.␀␀		Move the cursor and activate buttons with a␀		click of the left mouse button.␀␀		Activate pull-down menus by clicking the␀		menu title with either mouse button.␀␀		Select directories and files for backup,␀		restore, and compare, or any items from a list,␀		with a click of the right mouse button.␀␀		You can select a group of list items by holding␀		the right mouse button and dragging the cursor␀		over the list items you want to select.␀␀		NOTE:  Double-clicking the left mouse button␀		       is equivalent to single-clicking the␀			   right button.␀␀		Scroll rapidly through lists by holding the␀		left mouse button down, and moving the mouse␀		pointer up-above or down-below the list.␀␀		Scroll through lists by clicking the arrows␀		in the scroll bar, clicking and dragging the␀		slider box or clicking above or below the␀		slider box.␀␀		Cancel the current operation and return to the␀		previous dialog box by double-clicking the␀		system box in the upper left corner of the␀		current	dialog box.  Exit from Backup by double-␀        clicking the system box in the upper left corner␀        of the screen.␀␀For more information, see:␀␀	|␀Working With Backup Dialog Boxes|␀␀␀␀6oÉ>hi–ÃèJjk¶·Ëİìü9J^_—˜¬­Ş"#XÂÃñ Pno¾ìûü)Wkl˜Áí	G	H	v	Ÿ	É	õ	

