)*[Œ¹ËÌş;QR…µÔÕéê,-^Ÿ Ïş/a‘ÃÄÅÕÖ,-c›ÏEFx¥¦ÔÕûü&'Xhij‹Œ¬­Àà␀ @`€µèNxy¦§ÍÎÿ␀1ABCRS‰ºï01[\“Éğñ;r©à=u†‡›œÏÚÛóô&Wde›Ğ   G } ~ £ ¤ Ó Ô !.!Z![!’!µ!¶!·!ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀WORKING WITH BACKUP DIALOG BOXES␀ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀All Backup screens are displayed as dialog boxes. Dialog␀boxes are:␀␀	Screens which can accept information from you,␀	then act on the information you provide.␀␀	NOTE:  If you choose the Cancel button, the␀		   selections you make within a dialog box␀		   are discarded, and the settings␀		   are reset to their original values.␀␀ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ␀SELECTING ITEMS IN A DIALOG BOX␀␀The following items can be used to make selections␀in Backup dialog boxes:␀␀	ù  Command Buttons␀	ù  Title Buttons␀	ù  List Boxes␀	ù  Check Boxes␀	ù  Radio Buttons (Option Boxes)␀	ù  Text Boxes (Edit Boxes)␀	ù  System Boxes␀	ù  Pull-down Menus␀␀Each one of these items has a specific use and purpose.␀␀  ş	Command Buttons␀␀   	Are used to start an operation or accept the␀   	settings in the current dialog box.  They appear␀   	like this:␀␀   	ÚÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ¿ÚÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ¿␀   	³     Delete Files     ³³   Copy All Files   ³␀   	ÀÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÙÀÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÙ␀␀   		The button with the arrows is called the␀   		default button.  If you press Enter, this␀   		button will be activated regardless of the␀   		current cursor location.␀␀   		Choosing a Command Button:␀␀   				Place the mouse pointer on the button␀   				and click with the left or right mouse␀   				button.␀␀   				Move the highlight (cursor) onto the␀   				button with the Tab or Arrow keys, and␀   				press Enter.␀␀   				Hold down the Alt key and press the␀   				hotkey for the button you want to␀   				select.  The hotkey is the character␀   				within the button text which appears␀   				highlighted or in a contrasting color.␀␀   		NOTE:	When a button is unselectable, the␀   				word(s) on the button will not be␀   				capitalized.  The button cannot be␀   			    chosen until other selections are␀   			    changed or conditions change.␀␀  ş Title Buttons␀␀    Are used for making choices within a list of␀    mutually exclusive items.  When you select a title␀    button, a dialog box is opened that contains a␀    group of options.␀␀    Title buttons differ from other buttons in that the␀    hotkey which activates the button is in the Title␀    above the button.  Also, the current setting is␀    shown on the button.  They appear like this:␀␀   	    	   Backup Type:␀   			  ÚÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ¿␀   			  ³         Full         ³␀   			  ÀÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÙ␀␀   	In this example, the Backup Type setting is Full,␀   	and choosing this button would open a dialog box␀   	in which any Backup Type could be selected.␀␀   	To choose a Title Button:␀␀   			Place the mouse pointer on the button␀   			and click with the left or right mouse␀   			button.␀␀   			Move the highlight (cursor) onto the␀   			button with the Tab or Arrow keys, and␀   			press Enter.␀␀   			Hold down the Alt key and press the␀   			hotkey for the button you want to choose.␀   			The hotkey is the highlighted character␀   			within the title above the button.␀␀  ş List Boxes␀␀   	Are used to display a variety of information which␀   	often changes.  In Backup, list boxes are used to␀    display	disk, directory and file names.␀␀   				ÚÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ¿␀   				³    List Items:   ³␀   				ÃÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ´␀   				³^  Apple         ^ ^^³␀   				³û Banana         Û³ <ÄÄÄ Scroll Bar␀   				³  Grape          °³␀   				³û Pear           °³␀   				³  Watermelon     ^^³␀   				ÀÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÙ␀␀   	You will use list boxes to select drives,␀   	directories, and files for backup, compare, and␀    restore.␀␀   		Mouse Tips:␀␀   			Scroll rapidly through a list by holding␀   			the left mouse button down, and moving the␀   			mouse pointer up or down through the list.␀␀   			Select multiple items by holding the right␀   			mouse button down, and moving the mouse␀   			pointer up or down.  All items selected in␀   			this way will change to the state of the␀   			first item in the group.␀␀   			For example, if the first item is selected␀   			then all items are selected.  If the first␀   			item is deselected, then all items are␀   			deselected.␀␀   			Scroll the list by clicking the scroll bar␀   			arrows.␀␀   			Move the list by clicking and dragging␀   			the slider box.␀␀   			Move the list a page up or down by clicking␀   			the mouse pointer in the scroll bar above␀   			or below the slider box.␀␀   		Keyboard Tips:␀␀   			Tab will move the cursor into and out of a␀   			list box.␀␀   			Select items in a list box with Spacebar.␀   			Selected items are toggled on and off with␀   			Spacebar.␀␀   			In a list box, move the cursor directly␀   			to the item you want by starting to type␀   			the name of the item.  For example, typing␀    		"P" would move the cursor to the first item␀    		that begins with P, and	typing "Pe" would␀    		move to the first item that begins with Pe.␀␀␀  ş	Check Boxes␀␀   	Appear as squares within a dialog box, and are used␀	to toggle options on or off.␀␀   	The text next to a check box describes the option␀   	which can be on or off.  If you see a checkmark (û)␀   	in the check box, then the option is turned on.␀   	If no checkmark appears in the box, the option is␀   	turned off.␀␀   		For example:	[û] High Resolution - 300dpi␀␀   		In this example, the option is turned on and␀   		printer	output will be High Resolution.␀␀   	To select or deselect a check box option:␀␀   			Click the item with the mouse.␀␀   			Or, press the hotkey for the item.␀␀   			Or, move the cursor to the item and press␀   			Spacebar.␀␀␀  ş	Radio Buttons (Option Boxes)␀␀   	Appear in groups like this:␀␀   			 Flag Color:␀   			ÚÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ¿␀   			³ ( ) Red, White & Blue ³␀   			³ ( ) Green & Brown     ³␀   			³ () Black & Red       ³␀   			³ ( ) Yellow & Green    ³␀   			ÀÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÙ␀␀   	Radio buttons are mutually exclusive.  Only one␀    choice in the group can be selected at a time.␀    The Flag Color option box above contains four␀   	mutually exclusive choices; only one flag color␀   	can be chosen from the group of four.␀␀   	To select one of the items in the group:␀␀   			Click the item with the mouse.␀␀   			Or, press the hotkey letter for the item.␀␀   			Or, move the cursor to the item and press␀   			Spacebar.␀␀␀  ş	Text Boxes␀␀   	Are areas on the screen where you can enter text,␀	such as a filename or a directory path. In many␀	cases default text will appear in a text box, which␀	you may accept or overwrite.␀␀␀   	Text boxes appear like this:␀␀   			[TEXT BOXúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúúú]␀␀    To move the cursor to a text box in order to start␀    typing in it, use Tab or the arrow keys, or press␀	the hotkey in the text above the box.␀␀  ş System Boxes␀␀    Are used to cancel the current operation and return␀    to the previous dialog box. The system box appears␀    as a square in the upper left corner of the dialog␀    box.  Double-clicking the system box is equivalent␀    to choosing the Cancel button.␀␀    The title bar at the top of the screen also contains␀    a system box.  Double-click this system box to exit␀    from Backup.␀␀  ş	Pull-down Menus␀␀    Many of the Backup dialog boxes have pull-down␀    menus.␀␀    To activate a menu:␀␀    	Click the name of the menu, in the menu bar␀    	at the top of the screen, with either mouse␀    	button.␀␀    	Or, hold the Alt key while you press the hotkey␀    	letter for that menu.  The hotkey letter is the␀    	one that appears highlighted or in a contrasting␀    	color.␀␀    	Once you have opened one menu, you can open a␀    	different menu by using RightArrow or LeftArrow.␀␀    To choose an item from the menu:␀␀    	Click the item with either mouse button.␀␀    	Or, press the hotkey for that item.  The␀    	hotkey letter is the one that appears␀    	highlighted or in a contrasting color.␀␀    	Or, move the cursor to the item by using UpArrow␀  		or DownArrow, and press Enter.␀␀␀␀y␀ô␀-Y’Ä÷,abš¨©¿Àö÷"0EZ[qr¤ÖøùFz®·¸ÑÒ>q¦§½¾ë!123kyz±è %&=>nŸÒö÷+_’›œ¬­à	G	}	±	¾	¿	ñ	 
